  "problem": "Liam wants to paint a fence. He knows he needs $2$ liters of paint for $32$ square meters of fence. He creates a ratio table to determine the ratio of the volume of paint to the fenced area for different quantities.\n\n| Fence area (square meters) | Paint (liters) |\n| --- | --- |\n| $32$ | $2$ |\n| $80$ | $?$ |\n| $160$ | $10$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nWhat volume of paint does Liam need to paint $80$ square meters of the fence?",
